{"uid":"b2ab7198347927d1","name":"test_job_config_load_reads_job_yaml_the_agent_uid_cannot_open","fullName":"tests.test_job_config_defaults#test_job_config_load_reads_job_yaml_the_agent_uid_cannot_open","historyId":"f88337536ece99780e6bd36ad4cfbd2c","time":{"start":1791867273179,"stop":1791867273180,"duration":1},"description":"Task 023 (#180, requirement E.1): `/config` is a host directory\n    `ralphctl start` chmod's 0700 and leaves owned by whichever host uid ran\n    it -- under the uid boundary (`privsep.separate_engine_identity()`) the\n    engine's *effective* uid is the agent's, so a host uid other than the\n    agent's leaves the mount unreadable at that effective uid alone.\n    Modelled the same way `test_run_secrets.py` models a root-only MAC-key\n    file: `job.yaml` is chmod 0o000 (genuinely unreadable at this uid,\n    skipped when the suite itself runs as root), and the boundary is put in\n    force with the same stand-in for `privsep.root_for_write()` -- it\n    records that the elevation window was entered and, for its duration,\n    makes the file readable again, modelling root's exemption from the mode\n    check rather than reimplementing anything the production path does.\n    `JobConfig.load()` must still return the file's contents, and the file\n    must be exactly as unreadable again once the read returns.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 023 (#180, requirement E.1): <code>/config</code> is a host directory<br />\n<code>ralphctl start</code> chmod's 0700 and leaves owned by whichever host uid ran<br />\nit -- under the uid boundary (<code>privsep.separate_engine_identity()</code>) the<br />\nengine's <em>effective</em> uid is the agent's, so a host uid other than the<br />\nagent's leaves the mount unreadable at that effective uid alone.<br />\nModelled the same way <code>test_run_secrets.py</code> models a root-only MAC-key<br />\nfile: <code>job.yaml</code> is chmod 0o000 (genuinely unreadable at this uid,<br />\nskipped when the suite itself runs as root), and the boundary is put in<br />\nforce with the same stand-in for <code>privsep.root_for_write()</code> -- it<br />\nrecords that the elevation window was entered and, for its duration,<br />\nmakes the file readable again, modelling root's exemption from the mode<br />\ncheck rather than reimplementing anything the production path does.<br />\n<code>JobConfig.load()</code> must still return the file's contents, and the file<br />\nmust be exactly as unreadable again once the read returns.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791866910604,"stop":1791866910605,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791866910605,"stop":1791866910605,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791867273159,"stop":1791867273159,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791867273159,"stop":1791867273165,"duration":6},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791867273165,"stop":1791867273166,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep